			"original_statement": "The term 'engineering' has its roots in the Latin word 'ingenium,' meaning innate quality, especially mental power, and 'ingeniare,' to contrive, devise. It began to take its modern form in the 14th century, fundamentally associated with the designing and building of engines and technical constructions."
